  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Runtime",
      "items": [
        "A client-only single-page app: no server code in this repo",
        "A HashRouter serves /, /projects and /terminal; unknown addresses go home",
        "Home, Projects and Terminal share symmetric page padding (120px top and bottom) and one glass-panel class from src/styles/glass.css, so each panel is centred on the window's middle line, level with the centred site menu",
        "The home panel holds the name, the role subline and the newest project (projects[0]); the name button toggles the cat. Four hidden Poke Balls are spread over the panel and come last in document and tab order",
        "Home, the social bar and the terminal read the name, role and links from src/data/profile.ts",
        "The only persisted state is the colour index in localStorage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Terminal",
      "items": [
        "A fake shell in plain React on /terminal: type a command, read the answer",
        "The logic is pure and unit-tested: parser, commands, shell, virtual filesystem and Tab completion import nothing from React; Terminal.tsx is the view and carries out the effects",
        "Command names, play skip, theme names and open targets ignore case, and Tab completes them from any case; file paths stay case-sensitive",
        "The scrollback (500 lines), the folder and the history (500 commands) live in a SessionProvider above the routes, so they survive a visit to another page. Memory only: a reload starts a fresh session",
        "The virtual filesystem is generated from the data modules, so a new project, job or school becomes a file with no further change",
        "play returns a game effect and Terminal.tsx switches the pane to the Game (a finished game starts again); play skip prints the career as text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Game: Career Quest",
      "items": [
        "A Game Boy style adventure on a 160x144 canvas inside the terminal panel; the maps, people and battles are built from the same data as the virtual filesystem",
        "The engine is pure: step(state, input, world) returns the next state plus text events and sound cues. useGameLoop runs it at a fixed 60 ticks a second on requestAnimationFrame, capping a stalled frame at 100 ms; with reduced motion each press is one whole move",
        "The title has three rows, START, MODE and LIGHT. The engine only asks for a mode or light change by a cue; the Game component switches the setting and redraws, as on the Settings tab",
        "It starts as a Game Boy Color with the dim screen: the green sheets are recoloured once per palette, and dimmed copies are made the first time DIM is wanted",
        "Progress and settings (sound, volume, LCD look, mode, light) live in the terminal session, in memory only: leaving the game or the page keeps them, a reload starts at the title with the defaults",
        "The canvas is hidden from assistive technology; a polite live region tells the story, and Skip to text prints the career",
        "Pixel art is generated: scripts/sprites turns pixel definitions into three indexed PNG sheets and atlas.ts, and npm run sprites -- --check fails when they differ"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Sound",
      "items": [
        "Synthesised on Web Audio with no audio files: scores are text and a sequencer hands out notes just ahead of the clock",
        "The director picks the tune for each moment (title, map, battle, fanfare, ending); notes missed in a page stall are left out instead of starting all at once",
        "A player piano in the cafe plays any of twelve pieces, levelled to the cafe tune; its piece carries on where the game has it after the sound comes back or the game is entered again",
        "One player per visit, paused while the tab is hidden; a missing AudioContext never reaches the game"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Theme",
      "items": [
        "The matrix colour and the site theme are one index, owned by ThemeProvider",
        "cycle and select store the index; preview shows a theme for now without storing it, and a real choice ends it",
        "main.tsx applies the stored theme before React renders, then turns the fade on",
        "CSS files read --accent tokens on html, the shared glass stylesheet included; clicking the rain changes them all"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Delivery and tests",
      "items": [
        "Every push and pull request runs check, build and e2e; deploy needs all three and runs only on main",
        "The custom domain and HTTPS live in the Pages settings, not in a file",
        "Vitest unit tests sit beside the code in src/, including the game's engine, content, renderer, palettes, loop and audio",
        "Playwright tests a fresh production build (CI: the exact dist of the build job) on desktop and mobile; the game pilot plays by key presses and steps a copy of the engine alongside, so a test can ask for a place or a solved puzzle instead of listing keys"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
